.TH PVE\-ROLLING\-UPGRADE 8 "2026-06-16" "1.0.0" "Proxmox VE Tools"
.SH NAME
pve\-rolling\-upgrade \- rolling, health\-gated Proxmox VE 8\(->9 upgrade of one cluster node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-rolling\-upgrade
.RI [ options ]
.I node
.br
.B pve\-rolling\-upgrade
.RB [ \-\-jump
.IR user @ host ]
.RB [ \-\-stable
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-target
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-nic\-pin
.IR keep | pmx ]
.I node
.br
.B pve\-rolling\-upgrade
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.I node
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-rolling\-upgrade
upgrades a single Proxmox VE node from 8.x to 9.x (Debian Bookworm to Trixie)
in a rolling, health\-gated way and \fBwithout shutting guests down\fR. It
live\-migrates every running guest off the node, rewrites the APT repositories
from
.I bookworm
to
.IR trixie ,
runs the distribution upgrade, pins the network\-interface names and hardens the
boot path, reboots, and only reports success once a full health gate passes
(NIC names, bonds and BGP\-EVPN, Ceph
.IR active+clean ,
and monitor quorum).
.PP
It operates on
.B one node at a time
and is meant to be driven from a controller or jump host. Run it on the cluster
in the correct order \(em non\-monitor nodes first, the monitor
.B leader last
\(em re\-checking cluster health between nodes. Every site\-specific value
(stable peer for cluster checks, migration targets, expected monitor\-quorum
size, target kernel, which repository files carry
.IR bookworm ,
and whether FRR/EVPN is in use) is
.B auto\-discovered
from the live cluster.
.PP
The tool
.B hard\-stops
(non\-zero exit) on any failed pre\-condition or gate, so a problem halts at the
current node instead of cascading across the cluster.
.SH SAFETY
.B This is a production, hard\-to\-reverse operation: it reboots the target node.
With
.B \-\-dry\-run
the tool performs only read\-only discovery and prints the actions it would take.
The following pre\-conditions must already hold and are
.B not
established by this tool: every node already on the latest 8.4; Ceph (if
hyper\-converged) already on the release required by PVE 9; the
.I noout
flag set for the upgrade window; cluster health acceptable (only the
.I noout
warning); and a console/IPMI path available in case a reboot renames a NIC.
Per\-node guest live\-migration is HA\-aware (HA guests are moved with
.BR ha\-manager (1)).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jump " " \fIuser\fR@\fIhost\fR
ProxyJump/bastion host used to reach the cluster.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stable " " \fIhost\fR
Peer node used for cluster\-wide checks (Ceph, quorum). Default: auto\-discover
the first other cluster member.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-target " " \fIhost\fR
Migration target for the drain step. May be given multiple times. Default: all
other cluster members (guests are spread round\-robin).
.TP
.BR \-\-nic\-pin " " \fIkeep\fR|\fIpmx\fR
NIC naming policy across the kernel/systemd change.
.I keep
(default) pins the
.B current
names (e.g.
.IR eno* / ens5f* )
by permanent MAC via
.IR /etc/systemd/network/10\-pin\-*.link ;
.I pmx
uses
.BR pve\-network\-interface\-pinning (8),
which renames interfaces to the PVE
.I nicN
scheme.
.TP
.BR \-\-target\-kernel " " \fIVER\fR
Override the auto\-detected post\-upgrade kernel version used for the boot\-entry
and reboot gates.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Discover and print the intended actions without changing anything.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour (also disabled automatically when stdout is not a TTY).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
OK \(em the node was upgraded and every gate passed.
.TP
.B 1
FAIL \(em a pre\-condition or gate failed and the run halted. The node may be
mid\-upgrade; inspect it before continuing the rollout.
.TP
.B 2
USAGE \(em bad invocation, a missing dependency, or the node was unreachable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Overrides may be set in the environment or in
.IR /etc/pve\-rolling\-upgrade.conf
(a sourced shell file).
.TP
.B PVE_RU_SSH_OPTS
Extra
.BR ssh (1)
options (e.g.
.RI ' \-J\ admin@jump\ \-i\ ~/.ssh/key ').
.TP
.B PVE_RU_JUMP
Convenience ProxyJump host (same as
.BR \-\-jump ).
.TP
.B PVE_RU_KEEP_NIC_NAMES
.I 1
(default) keep current NIC names;
.I 0
use the
.I nicN
scheme (same as
.BR \-\-nic\-pin ).
.TP
.B PVE_RU_TARGET_KERNEL
Override the auto\-detected target kernel.
.TP
.B PVE_RU_VENDOR_HEALTH
Post\-reboot vendor health probe command (default: try
.B racadm getsysinfo
when present, on Dell hardware).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Dry\-run a node through a bastion (no changes):
.PP
.RS
.EX
pve\-rolling\-upgrade \-\-dry\-run \-j root@bastion 192.168.0.14
.EE
.RE
.PP
Upgrade the non\-monitor node first, keeping original NIC names:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pve\-rolling\-upgrade \-j root@bastion 192.168.0.14
.EE
.RE
.PP
Upgrade a node using the PVE
.I nicN
naming scheme instead:
.PP
.RS
.EX
pve\-rolling\-upgrade \-\-nic\-pin pmx pve04
.EE
.RE
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Controller:
.BR bash ", " ssh .
Each node: the PVE stack
.RB ( qm ", " pvecm ", " ceph ", " proxmox\-boot\-tool ),
.BR ethtool ;
FRR/EVPN gates run only when FRR is present. Key\-based root SSH to every node
(directly or through
.BR \-\-jump )
is assumed.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pve\-sdn\-healthcheck (8),
.BR pve\-vmnic\-fix (8),
.BR pve\-network\-interface\-pinning (8),
.BR ha\-manager (1),
.BR proxmox\-boot\-tool (1)
